<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trois-Rivières</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trois-Rivières is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, where the Saint-Maurice river meets the St Lawrence, halfway between Quebec City and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a>. Founded in 1634 by Laviolette on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain">Samuel de Champlain</a>'s orders, it was the second permanent French settlement on the St Lawrence and a fur-trading post. It later became an industrial centre known for pulp and paper.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trois-rivieres.jpg" alt="Trois-Rivières" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trois-Rivi%C3%A8res,_Quebec_(cropped)2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
